corpus_mapper/
corpus_mapper_output/

# Local pattern-list file for an internal content-safety scan. NEVER commit this file.
/.masking_patterns

# Keyed attestation material for the content-safety scan. Env-held, gitignored;
# rotating it invalidates every previously recorded attestation, so it is not
# rotated casually.
/.masking_attest_key

# Phase 133 baked atlas asset (offline bake output). Lives OUTSIDE web/static/
# on purpose -- the /static mount at web/main.py:740 serves web/static/
# publicly, which would let the asset bypass the atlas-preview feature flag.
# scp'd to the server like the other sidecar DBs; never committed.
/atlas_data/

# Phase 134 (Discovery Data Spine) built sidecar payload: discovery.db (+ any
# schema-versioned siblings) plus the offline distillation's review/frame
# artifacts. Never commit the built .db -- like the other sidecar DBs
# (pgp.db, fjms_enrichment.db, atlas_data/), it is scp'd to the server /
# bundled with the desktop installer, not tracked in git (DATA-08 deploy
# posture: temp upload -> verify -> atomic rename -> code deploy).
/discovery_data/

# Discovery BUILD depot: the intermediate and candidate artifacts a discovery
# bake produces (reference corpora, match databases, private/public candidate
# sidecars, preview copies, per-run manifests). Relocated here from /_tmp/ on
# 2026-08-16 for one reason: /_tmp/ is this repo's SCRATCH directory -- CLAUDE.md
# and scripts/init.ps1 both describe it as "working notes" and init.ps1 lists its
# contents as ephemera -- and the V4 depot sitting in it included the local twin
# of the artifact production serves, 10.9 GB whose content hash matches its own
# asset_basename. Nothing had deleted it; the point is that clearing scratch is a
# routine act and this was not scratch. Ignored for the same reason as
# /discovery_data/: built payloads are scp'd, never committed. NOTE this is still
# inside the working tree, so `git clean -xfd` would remove it exactly as it
# would /discovery_data/ and /atlas_data/.
/discovery_builds/

# discovery-v3 bake run state (module kept in the private repository). Per-run,
# per-machine progress ledgers + their interrupted-write temp files. Already
# covered by the /discovery_data/ and /_tmp/ rules above, but named explicitly
# and without a leading slash so a state file written to ANY directory is
# ignored: it is per-machine run state that must never be committed, and it
# can carry step names and messages.
v3_bake_state*.json
v3_bake_state*.json.*.tmp
*.bake_state.json
*.bake_state.json.*.tmp

# Scratch transcripts from external review tools; never committed.
tmp/CODEX-*
tmp/codex_*
/tmp/

# ── Local research corpora, runtime sidecars, and root scratch ──
# Ignoring only — nothing already tracked is untracked by this block.

# Saved puzzle/join documents sidecar (joins.db + its WAL/SHM).
# NEVER TRACK THIS — it is not merely hygiene, it is a data-loss guard.
# PuzzleService creates the dir and schema at runtime (shared/puzzle_service.py
# mkdir at ~L97), so the repo never needs to supply it; locally it is an empty
# scratch DB. But on the WEB SERVER this same repo-root path holds the LIVE,
# shared, user-created join documents (web/pages/puzzle.py ~L2247), and
# deploy.sh runs `git reset --hard origin/$BRANCH`. reset --hard spares
# untracked/ignored files but clobbers tracked ones — so a committed joins.db
# would wipe every join users saved since that commit, on every deploy.
# (Frozen desktop is unaffected: it uses %LOCALAPPDATA%\GenizahSearchPro\.)
/joins_data/

# PGP raw text dump (~317 MB), sibling of the already-ignored `pgp_data/*.db`
# above. Scoped to the subdirectory: pgp_data/full_import_report.txt and
# pgp_data/import_report.csv REMAIN TRACKED.
pgp_data/pgp-text/

# Desktop session backup of the Tantivy index directory — carries LocalIndex/,
# app logs, and a config.pkl holding per-user desktop state. `Genizah_Index/`
# is ignored above (the bare `Genizah_Index/` rule); this is the differently-named backup twin.
/Genizah_Index.session-bak/

# Ad-hoc analysis output directory (per-run subfolders).
/outputs/

# Joins Lab candidate exports — regenerated on demand by the lab's XLSX export.
/joins_lab_candidates*.xlsx

# cairo-genizah-research skill runtime state (self-throttle bookkeeping).
# Narrow by design: the state/ directory's tracked .gitkeep must survive.
skills/*/state/throttle.json

# Local passage-index build + evaluation output (parallel-search work). Multi-GB and
# machine-local; added 2026-08-20 after a release-time `git add -A` would have staged
# 3.6 GB of it from the repo root while a job was still writing to it.
passage_index/

# Work/author correction sheets for the private review artifact: generated from
# the db by scripts/export_work_authors.py and scripts/report_author_issues.py,
# edited by the owner, applied by scripts/apply_work_author_rulings.py. Every
# applied ruling lives in the artifact's own `work_author_ruling` table, so
# these files are working copies, not a record -- and they carry reference-work
# titles, which do not belong in the repo.
/work_authors*.csv

# Generated by a scheduler script kept in the private repository: absolute paths to
# ONE machine's python and repo, so it is per-machine, not shared.
scripts/nightly_verify_review_artifact.cmd
scripts/nightly_verify_search_combinations.cmd

# ── Tracked files that an earlier blanket rule above also matches (2026-09-18) ──────
# An ignore rule is inert for a path git already tracks, so these have been fine -- until
# one is deleted and regenerated, or a clean clone tries to `git add` it: then the blanket
# rule wins silently. Negating them here (after every rule that matches them) keeps them
# addable. Verify with `git check-ignore --no-index -v <path>` (prints nothing = addable).
!/GenizahSearchPro.spec
!/char_merges_report.xlsx
!/fist_gap_rows.csv
!/fist_gap_manifest.txt
!/bodleian_master_index.csv
!/reports/leading_zero_collisions.csv
!/reports/synthetic_parent_shelfmarks.csv
!/reports/cudl_full_normalization_collisions.csv
!/reports/cudl_resolution_changes_2026-10-29.csv

# Written by deploy.sh on the server AFTER a successful restart: the revision the
# running genizah-web actually loaded. Per-machine runtime state, never committed.
/.deployed_revision

# Blau dictionary sidecar (docs/plans/BLAU_DICTIONARY_PLAN.md): the download under
# blau_data/download/ is untrusted third-party data fetched by hand, and blau.db is the
# build artifact of scripts/build_blau_sidecar.py, deployed like the other *_data/ sidecars.
blau_data/

# Arabic dictionary sidecar (docs/plans/ARABIC_DICTIONARY_LAYER_PLAN.md, phase A): the download
# under arabic_data/download/ is untrusted third-party data fetched by scripts/build_arabic_sidecar.py
# fetch, and arabic.db is its build artifact, deployed like the other *_data/ sidecars.
arabic_data/

# Friedman dictionary source archive and extraction candidates (not a served sidecar).
friedman_data/

# Catalogue text search sidecar (docs/plans/CATALOGUE_TEXT_SEARCH_PLAN.md): catalog_text.db is
# DERIVED by scripts/build_catalog_text_sidecar.py from the FJMS and PGP sidecars, libraries.csv and
# libraries_translations.db, rebuilt after every refresh of any of them; never committed.
catalog_data/

# Private material lives in the private repository checked out BESIDE this one, never here.
.planning/
GenizahSearch-private/
# Kept in the private repository at the same path; scripts/generate_fist_gap_csv.py writes it here.
/fist_gap_ambiguous_titles.txt
# The owner-held discovery precision spec, copied into the checkout root on the server.
/discovery_precision_spec.json
